{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M7mHXitkWsfLEBY2GQyQkM","type":"tool_result","content":"1----\n2-name: spine-authoring\n3:description: Use when breaking down or developing the SN → SR → LLR → TC spine — the adjudicator's question list per tier: what a need must carry before it is approved, what belongs at SR versus LLR versus the trace tier, when an obligation is a labelled derived requirement, and which instruments catch a distorted breakdown.\n4-stacks: [python, node, powershell, go, rust, any]\n5-domains: [any]\n6-phases: [dev, gate]\n7-tags: [requirements, decomposition, tiering, derivation, hats, derived-requirements, acceptance-criteria]\n8-scope: kit\n9----\n10-\n11-# Spine authoring (breaking down SN → SR → LLR → TC)\n12-\n13-You are the **adjudicator**: the one deciding what a row says and which tier it\n14-says it at. Every mechanized check on the spine is a *detector* — it reports a\n15-smell after the fact. The tiering itself is a judgement, and this is the question\n--\n181-  adjudicator's judgement.\n182-- **(c) If the obligation arrived through a lens rather than the need's text,\n183:  RECORD the lens.** This is DO-178C's **derived requirement** class: content\n184-  beyond what the parent demands, legitimate *because* it is (i) recorded as\n185-  derived in a cell something reads, (ii) carrying a rationale that argues the\n186-  deriving lens — the hat, the design\n187-  constraint, the implementation fact — and (iii) fed back upward so the\n188-  need owner sees it. Name the deriving hat in **`Hat-Refs`** (roster names; the\n189-  cell IS the row's perspective record, and a name the roster does not declare is a\n190-  finding) and argue it in `Rationale`. A prose label alone is not the record: it\n191-  resolves against nothing, so nothing can tell a retired hat from a live one.\n192-  **Never silently trace a derived row to a\n193-  parent whose text does not demand it**: that is the single most common way a\n194-  spine acquires structure nobody asked for and nobody can audit.\n195-  - A row derivable **only** through a hat that ships switched OFF must say so.\nSR-154 ['SN-026', 'SN-024', 'SN-006'] ['B-09', 'B-10'] ['UNATTENDED-OPS'] 1 Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions � every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, b\r\nSR-234 ['SN-006'] ['B-09', 'B-10'] ['UNATTENDED-OPS'] 6 A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-006 asks an unattended run to report failures clearly and surface to a human when it cannot proceed, but it does not state who ends a contested or repeated r\r\nSR-235 ['SN-024'] ['B-05'] ['INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY'] 6 A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-024 requires an independent critical eye and assigns the attended reviewer to the human, but does not require that verdict to survive as review history. The \r\nSR-233 ['SN-006'] ['B-09', 'B-10'] ['UNATTENDED-OPS'] 6 A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-006 requires an unattended run to report failures clearly and to continue until it must surface to a human; it does not say which hostile host conditions a r\r\nSR-155 ['SN-024', 'SN-006', 'SN-026', 'SN-002'] ['B-01', 'B-09', 'B-10'] ['UNATTENDED-OPS'] 4 Realizes SN-024 (a decomposition judged by a competing plan and an independent arbiter rather than its author), with SN-026 (the planner pair prefers distinct families), SN-002 (the selected outcome l","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1fb1008-6d93-4693-a49f-a0783f483182","uuid":"ce8ab848-dc38-4b01-9fc7-b0023390dc7c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:05:59.874Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1----\n2-name: spine-authoring\n3:description: Use when breaking down or developing the SN → SR → LLR → TC spine — the adjudicator's question list per tier: what a need must carry before it is approved, what belongs at SR versus LLR versus the trace tier, when an oblig